.\"
.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt NEWFS_APFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm newfs_apfs
.Nd construct a new Apple File System (APFS)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v Ar volume_name
.Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility destructively creates an APFS container with one initial volume on
the specified
.Ar device .
The target may be a regular file, block device, or character device with a
reported media size. Existing data on the target will no longer be accessible
as a filesystem after formatting; the utility does not securely erase the
entire target.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl v Ar volume_name
Specify the name of the initial APFS volume.
If not specified, "Untitled" is used.
.El
.Pp
This implementation creates a 4 KiB-block, single-volume APFS container.
The volume is unencrypted and unsealed. The target size must be a multiple of
4096 bytes and at least 1 MiB. Multi-volume, encrypted, sealed, and other
block-size configurations are not supported. The maximum size is limited by
the Space Manager CIB address table.
.Pp
Only run
.Nm
on a target whose contents may be destroyed. An I/O error can leave the target
unmountable.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount_apfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in NetBSD 11.0.
